Model marks
===========

What is here
  svg/*.svg     the provider icons boopis draws beside a model's name: a mono variant (currentColor) for each,
                and a colour variant where the source has one. Optimised with SVGO 3.3.2 (multipass, precision 2,
                viewBox kept, title, size and inline style removed, gradient ids prefixed).
  svg/generic.svg   boopis's own neutral mark for a model whose family is unknown. Not from the source below.
  map.json      which family a model id belongs to, and the brand-colour legibility rule.
  build.js      writes icons.js (node vendor/model-icons/build.js, no dependencies).
  icons.js      generated from map.json and svg/*.svg so pages opened from file:// can draw them. Do not edit.
                In the colour variants, a fill under 3:1 against the menu row keeps its hue and moves in OKLab
                lightness until it reaches 3:1, per scheme, through light-dark(); the shipped value stays as the
                fill attribute.

